      "type": "cleardrive-user-guide",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "Get to know your Digital mirror.",
        "intro": "Set up your mirror, find the view you like, and know how to save a recording when it matters.",
        "manual_url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0825/1051/2365/files/ClearDrive_19_Series_User_Manual_EN.pdf?v=1788642443",
        "installation_url": "/pages/self-installation",
        "contact_url": "shopify://pages/contact"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "setup_card": {"type":"setup","settings":{"number":"01","title":"Insert the memory card.","body":"<p>With the mirror powered off, insert a compatible high-endurance microSD card until it clicks into place. Choose Class 10 or faster, with a capacity supported by your exact model.</p><p>Stop recording and power off before removing the card.</p>"}},
        "setup_format": {"type":"setup","settings":{"number":"02","title":"Power on and format.","body":"<p>Start the vehicle. The mirror powers on automatically and begins recording. Before your first drive, open <strong>Home → Quick Access → Format Card</strong> and confirm.</p><p><strong>Formatting erases everything on the card, including locked clips.</strong> Back up existing files first.</p>"}},
        "setup_time": {"type":"setup","settings":{"number":"03","title":"Set your local time.","body":"<p>Go to <strong>Home → Settings → System → Date / Time</strong>. Set the correct local date and time so you can find recordings by their timestamps.</p><p>Check it again after vehicle power has been disconnected.</p>"}},
        "setup_view": {"type":"setup","settings":{"number":"04","title":"Check the view and recording.","body":"<p>Return to <strong>Driving Recorder</strong>. Confirm the rear image is level, clear and unobstructed. On dual-camera models, swipe left or right to check each view.</p><p>Check that recording is active before driving.</p>"}},
        "setting_loop": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Change the length of each video clip","path":"Settings → Recording → Loop Recording","body":"<p>Choose <strong>1, 3 or 5 minutes</strong> per clip. The mirror saves your journey in separate files instead of one long video.</p><p>This controls each clip's length, not the total amount of video your card holds. As the card fills, older normal recordings are replaced. Locked clips need to be reviewed separately.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-loop-recording.webp"}},
        "setting_brightness": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Adjust brightness and screen-off timing","path":"Settings → System → Auto Brightness / Auto Screen Off","body":"<p><strong>Auto Brightness</strong> uses the ambient light sensor to adjust the screen. For manual control, turn it off and use the brightness slider on the live screen.</p><p><strong>Auto Screen Off</strong> lets you choose when the display turns off. A short press of the physical Power / Display button turns the screen off or back on.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-screen-off.webp"}},
        "setting_time": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Set date, time and on-screen information","path":"Settings → System → Date / Time; Settings → Watermark","body":"<p>Set the correct local date and time before recording. The mirror has no internal battery, so the clock may reset if vehicle power is disconnected.</p><p>Under <strong>Watermark</strong>, choose whether to display the date and time, recording icon and recording timer.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-date-time.webp"}},
        "setting_image": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Check the camera image orientation","path":"Settings → Recording → Camera Image","body":"<p>Choose <strong>Original</strong> or <strong>Mirrored</strong> for the camera image. These options change the left-to-right orientation.</p><p>While parked, check the displayed scene against your surroundings so the view is familiar before you drive.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-camera-image.webp"}},
        "setting_audio": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Control recording audio and system sounds","path":"Live screen → Microphone; Settings → System","body":"<p>The <strong>Microphone</strong> control determines whether sound is recorded with your video.</p><p><strong>Button Sound, Voice Prompts and Alert Volume</strong> control the mirror's system sounds. These are separate from the microphone setting.</p><p>If your menus are not in English, open <strong>Settings → System → Language</strong> and choose English.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-system.webp"}},
        "setting_card": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Look after the memory card","path":"Quick Access → Format Card; or Settings → System → Format Card","body":"<p>Back up important files and format the card in the mirror periodically to maintain reliable recording. Formatting permanently erases normal videos, locked videos and photos.</p><p>If errors or damaged files keep returning after formatting, replace the card with a compatible high-endurance Class 10 or faster card.</p>","image_asset":"cleardrive-guide-format-card.webp"}},
        "setting_version": {"type":"setting","settings":{"title":"Find your firmware version","path":"Quick Access → Version; or Settings → System → Firmware Version","body":"<p>Open Version to see the software revision installed on your mirror. Include this information when contacting ClearDrive support about menus, card compatibility or a recurring issue.</p><p><strong>Factory Reset</strong> is a separate System Settings option that restores settings to their factory defaults. Check your date, time and preferences again afterward.</p>"}},
        "faq_record": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"The mirror cannot record or shows a card error.","answer":"<p>Stop safely, stop recording and power the unit off before checking the microSD card. Reinsert it fully, then power on.</p><p>Back up any files you can still access before formatting the card in the mirror. If the error returns, replace it with a compatible high-endurance Class 10 or faster card.</p>"}},
        "faq_freeze": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"The touchscreen is frozen or the mirror is unresponsive.","answer":"<p>While safely parked, briefly press the <strong>Reset pinhole</strong> with a blunt pin less than 1 mm in diameter. Use light pressure; the unit restarts.</p><p>If freezing returns, back up important recordings, format the card in the device, or replace an unreliable card. Check that power connections are fully seated. Contact support if the issue continues.</p>"}},
        "faq_audio": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Why is there no sound in my saved video?","answer":"<p>First check the playback volume. If the microphone was off when the clip was recorded, that clip has no recorded audio. Turn <strong>Microphone On</strong> from the live screen before making new recordings.</p>"}},
        "faq_time": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Why did the date and time reset?","answer":"<p>The mirror is powered by the vehicle and has no internal battery. Disconnecting vehicle power can reset its clock.</p><p>Reconnect power, then open <strong>Settings → System → Date / Time</strong> and set the local date and time again.</p>"}},
        "faq_locked": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Why are there so many locked files?","answer":"<p>Impact detection and parking-monitor sensitivity can protect extra clips after vibration or door movement. Higher sensitivity may trigger more often.</p><p>Review and back up important Locked files, then remove unneeded clips. Check the collision and parking sensitivity settings. Locked files may not be overwritten by normal loop recording.</p>"}},
        "faq_parking": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Why is Parking Monitor not working?","answer":"<p>The feature requires a compatible vehicle-specific kit and constant-power connection. It also depends on available vehicle power, card capacity and firmware.</p><p>Check that Parking Monitor is not set to Off, then contact your ClearDrive installer to confirm the harness and power setup. Do not modify the wiring to enable the feature.</p>"}},
        "faq_card": {"type":"faq","settings":{"question":"Which microSD card should I use?","answer":"<p>Choose a <strong>high-endurance microSD / TF card, Class 10 or faster</strong>, rated for the capacity supported by your exact mirror model and firmware. Capacity limits differ by version; confirm compatibility before using a larger card.</p><p>Insert it with the power off and format it in the device before first use. If you are unsure, send your model and firmware version to ClearDrive support.</p>"}}
